  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Fill from the point (X, Y): changes all connected pixels of the colour of that point (target_colour) to current_colour, or to the dither colours. Uses a stack of 3-byte entries (direction, X, Y) from $c100. A press of the button stops the fill. Keeps brush_ptr, and sets dither_on to 0 at the end."},
    {"at":8,"placement":"side","text":"brush_ptr = $1868 during the fill."},
    {"at":30,"placement":"side","text":"target_colour = the colour of the start pixel."},
    {"at":36,"placement":"side","text":"Same colour: exchanges the dither colours 0/1 and 2/3. When it is still the same colour, the fill does nothing."},
    {"at":88,"placement":"side","text":"dither_on = 1 when the dither colours 0 and 1 differ."},
    {"at":100,"placement":"side","text":"Stack pointer = $c0fd: the stack is empty."},
    {"at":108,"placement":"side","text":"plot_vector = $17ad."},
    {"at":116,"placement":"side","text":"$3b/$3c = $38ca. The fill does not read it."},
    {"at":124,"placement":"side","text":"Paints the start pixel, then pushes its 4 neighbours."},
    {"at":139,"placement":"line","text":"Takes the last entry from the stack. When the pixel still has target_colour, paints it and pushes the neighbours, but not the neighbour that the entry came from."},
    {"at":139,"placement":"side","text":"A press stops the fill."},
    {"at":145,"placement":"side","text":"Stack pointer high byte $c0: the stack is empty."},
    {"at":184,"placement":"side","text":"Direction of the entry: 0 down, $80 right, $20 left, $40 up."},
    {"at":213,"placement":"line","text":"Moves the stack pointer (point_x1/point_y1) 3 bytes up."},
    {"at":225,"placement":"line","text":"Reads the entry at the stack pointer: cursor_y = byte 2, cursor_x = byte 1, A = byte 0 (the direction)."},
    {"at":240,"placement":"line","text":"Entry from the pixel above: pushes down, right and left."},
    {"at":253,"placement":"line","text":"Entry from the pixel to the left: pushes down, right and up."},
    {"at":266,"placement":"line","text":"Entry from the pixel to the right: pushes down, then left and up."},
    {"at":282,"placement":"line","text":"Entry from the pixel below: pushes right, then left and up."},
    {"at":298,"placement":"line","text":"When the pixel under (cursor_x, cursor_y) is in the picture (Y less than max_y) and has target_colour, pushes it with direction 0. Keeps cursor_y."},
    {"at":323,"placement":"line","text":"When the pixel to the right is in the picture (X less than max_x) and has target_colour, pushes it with direction $80. Keeps cursor_x."},
    {"at":348,"placement":"line","text":"When the pixel to the left is in the picture and has target_colour, pushes it with direction $20. Keeps cursor_x."},
    {"at":372,"placement":"line","text":"When the pixel above is in the picture and has target_colour, pushes it with direction $40. Keeps cursor_y."},
    {"at":396,"placement":"line","text":"Pushes the pixels to the left and above (as fill_push_left and fill_push_up), then goes back to fill_loop."},
    {"at":449,"placement":"line","text":"Pushes the entry (A = direction, cursor_x, cursor_y) on the fill stack. With the stack pointer in page $ce, it first removes the entries of filled pixels (fill_compact_stack). From $cff0 on, it does not push."},
    {"at":460,"placement":"line","text":"Pushes one fill entry (direction temp_word, cursor_x, cursor_y) at point_x1/point_y1 + 3, and moves the fill stack pointer. A = the high byte of the pointer. When the stack is full ($cff0 or higher), it pushes nothing."},
    {"at":499,"placement":"line","text":"Pushes the entry, then copies each stack entry whose pixel does not have current_colour to the bottom of the stack ($c100 on). The stack pointer becomes the end of the kept entries. Keeps cursor_x and cursor_y."},
    {"at":566,"placement":"line","text":"Exchanges the stack pointer (point_x1/point_y1) with circle_dx/$45."},
    {"at":587,"placement":"line","text":"Copies the 3 bytes of the entry at the stack pointer to point_x0/point_y0, and moves point_x0/point_y0 3 bytes up."},
    {"at":608,"placement":"line","text":"When the pixel (cursor_x, cursor_y) has target_colour, gets its dither colour (when dither_on) and paints it with fill_set_pixel. Z is clear when the pixel has an other colour."},
    {"at":650,"placement":"line","text":"Paints the pixel at pixel_ptr with current_colour: bit pair 0 for the background colour, else the bit pair that $1531 gives for the cell. With Mirror on, paints the 4 mirrored pixels with fill_set_pixel_mirror. Z is set at the end."},
    {"at":702,"placement":"line","text":"Plots the pixel (X, Y) and its mirror images (159 - X, Y), (159 - X, 199 - Y) and (X, 199 - Y) with $1841. Keeps cursor_x and cursor_y."},
    {"at":761,"placement":"line","text":"Reads the pixel (cursor_x, cursor_y) and gives its colour in A. When dither_on, current_colour becomes the dither colour of that point. Z is set when the colour is target_colour."}
  ],
